SUMMARY:John Mulaney: Mister Whatever LIVE at Wrigley Field
DTSTAMP:20260710T043049Z
DTSTART:20260711T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets\n \nAbout John Mulaney\nJohn Mul
	aney is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians of his generation. T
	he Emmy Award-winning writer and performer first rose to national prominen
	ce as a writer for Saturday Night Live\, before launching a stand-up caree
	r that has produced some of the most beloved comedy specials of the past d
	ecade — including New in Town\, The Comeback Kid\, Kid Gorgeous\, and Baby
	 J. \nKnown for his razor-sharp storytelling\, his impeccable timing\, and
	 his ability to turn deeply personal experiences into universally hilariou
	s comedy\, Mulaney has built one of the most devoted fan bases in stand-up
	. His Mister Whatever tour has been selling out arenas and stadiums across
	 North America\, and this Chicago date is the crown jewel of the entire ru
	n. \nOn July 11\, 2026\, John Mulaney will make history as the first comed
	ian to ever headline Wrigley Field — one of the most iconic sports and ent
	ertainment venues in the world. This is a once-in-a-lifetime event for Chi
	cago comedy fans. \nEvent Details\n\nEvent: John Mulaney: Mister Whatever\
	nDate: Saturday\, July 11\, 2026\nShow Time: 8:00 PM CT\nVenue: Wrigley Fi
	eld\nAddress: 1060 W Addison St\, Chicago\, IL 60613\nNote: Tickets are no
	n-transferable for this event\n\nAbout Wrigley Field\nWrigley Field is one
	 of the most iconic and beloved sports venues in the United States. Built 
	in 1914\, the home of the Chicago Cubs seats approximately 41\,000 fans an
	d is renowned for its ivy-covered outfield walls\, its classic manual scor
	eboard\, and its unmatched atmosphere in the heart of Chicago’s Wrigleyvil
	le neighborhood. \nHosting a comedy show at Wrigley Field is an unpreceden
	ted event — the historic ballpark has never before hosted a stand-up comed
	ian as a headliner. The venue is easily accessible via CTA Red Line (Addis
	on station) and is surrounded by bars\, restaurants\, and the vibrant ener
	gy of Wrigleyville. Parking is available in the surrounding neighborhood\,
	 though public transit is strongly recommended. \nWhat to Expect\nJohn Mul
	aney’s Mister Whatever is a full headline stand-up show featuring all-new 
	material. Expect the signature Mulaney experience — brilliantly crafted st
	orytelling\, perfectly timed punchlines\, and the kind of deeply personal 
	comedy that feels both intimate and epic\, even in a stadium setting. \nTh
	is is a historic night for Chicago comedy. Seeing John Mulaney perform sta
	nd-up at Wrigley Field is an experience that will be talked about for deca
	des. Arrive early to soak in the atmosphere of one of baseball’s most stor
	ied venues transformed into a comedy stage. \nTicket Information\nTickets 
	for John Mulaney: Mister Whatever at Wrigley Field start from $165. Purcha
	se official tickets through Ticketmaster or find resale tickets through Vi
	vidSeats. \n\nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets\n \nThis post contains affili
	ate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.\n\nhttps://co
	medycalendar.com/event/john-mulaney-mister-whatever-live-at-wrigley-field/
	\n\nFrom Comedy Calendar
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/john-mulaney-mister-whatever-live-at-w
	rigley-field/
LOCATION:Wrigley Field\, 1060 W Addison St\, Chicago\, IL\, 60613\, USA
